        "country": "IN",
        "summary": "Monitoring is on the owner: watch the public search portal and the weekly Trade Marks Journal — oppositions run for 4 months from publication of a conflicting application.",
        "actionUrl": "https://tmrsearch.ipindia.gov.in/tmrpublicsearch/",
        "actionLabel": "IP India — trade mark public search"
      },
      {
        "country": "UK",
        "summary": "The UK IPO notifies owners of earlier UK marks when a similar application publishes, but acting is on you: a 2-month opposition window (extendable by one) from publication in the journal.",
        "actionUrl": "https://www.gov.uk/search-for-trademark",
        "actionLabel": "UK IPO — search for a trade mark"
      },
      {
        "country": "DE",
        "summary": "The DPMA examines only absolute grounds and does not notify earlier owners — watching DPMAregister (or paying a watch service) is on you, with a 3-month opposition window after publication.",
        "actionUrl": "https://register.dpma.de/",
        "actionLabel": "DPMAregister (register & journal)"
      },
      {
        "country": "FR",
        "summary": "The INPI does not police conflicts for you: monitor the Bulletin officiel de la propriété industrielle via INPI's databases and oppose within 2 months of a conflicting publication.",
        "actionUrl": "https://www.inpi.fr/",
        "actionLabel": "INPI — marques"
      }
    ]
